    "freeTraits": 0,
    "biography": "<h2>Background</h2><p>A Mameluke warrior of Circassian origin, Mukhtar Bey was Embraced without a clan lineage (a @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.clans.JournalEntry.SNuXttNqxzJ6uPXv]{Caitiff}) by the childe of Sultan Antonius, the @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.clans.JournalEntry.OpCOs3PLjmtl0QVu]{Ventrue} prince he would go on to serve as sheriff. When the Lupines struck the sultan's court during the Night of the Long Knives in 1406, Mukhtar Bey froze in terror and fled, leaving his patron to die. Consumed by shame, he nonetheless accepted the princedom of Cairo when the city's Kindred turned to him afterward, and he has held it for over five centuries &mdash; enforcing the Traditions with genuine, if hollow, diligence.</p><p>As the Final Nights loom, Mukhtar Bey's cowardice has curdled into a monstrous survival scheme. The returned @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.clans.JournalEntry.4795a736271143af]{True @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.clans.JournalEntry.ZFYurbvAHfaRguYI]{Brujah}} elder Al-Muntaqim has convinced him that gathering Cairo's @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.clans.JournalEntry.SNuXttNqxzJ6uPXv]{Caitiff} population together &mdash; ostensibly as a haven and political voice via a khitta on Gezira and a seat on his Consultative Council &mdash; will let the two of them offer the entire clanless population of the city as a sacrifice to appease the awakening Antediluvians, sparing the prince and the Avenger alone. Mukhtar Bey has no idea that his own childer among the Caitiff, drawn to Cairo by his seeming generosity, are being fattened for slaughter.</p><h2>Roleplaying Hints</h2><p>Portray Mukhtar Bey as a once-formidable warrior whose regal bearing now rings hollow with terror he can never voice. He rules with real administrative competence &mdash; laying down law, keeping the Masquerade, mediating disputes &mdash; but flinches from any suggestion of confrontation with something genuinely dangerous, and he is quietly, desperately watching for any sign that Gehenna is at hand.</p>",
    "notes": "Sire: Wife of the Tiger and the Snake. Secretly conspiring with the @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.clans.JournalEntry.4795a736271143af]{True @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.clans.JournalEntry.ZFYurbvAHfaRguYI]{Brujah}} elder Al-Muntaqim to sacrifice Cairo's @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.clans.JournalEntry.SNuXttNqxzJ6uPXv]{Caitiff} population to the Antediluvians on the night of Gehenna, sparing themselves. Suspicious of his own @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.clans.JournalEntry.SNuXttNqxzJ6uPXv]{Caitiff} confederate Waulkeen, and watching the Caitiff of Zamalek closely. Merits/Flaws (as printed): Iron Will.",
    "npcType": "vampire"
  },
